NAME=git
VERSION=2.44.0
DESCRIPTION="Distributed version control system (HTTPS via curl --with-mbedtls; SSH via dropbear)"
CATEGORY=util
DEPS=zlib curl
URL=https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.44.0.tar.xz
SHA256=e358738dcb5b5ea340ce900a0015c03ae86e804e7ff64e47aa4631ddee681de3
MAINTAINER=m3os

# Phase 85b Track A: git is the first real cross-compiled toolchain on top of
# the Phase 85a `.m3pkg` packaging substrate. Phase 86c REBUILDS it WITH curl:
# the `NO_CURL` knob is removed and a static `libcurl --with-mbedtls` is linked,
# so `git clone https://github.com/…` works over real TLS (cert chain + hostname
# validated against the Phase 86a CA bundle). `NO_OPENSSL=1` stays — the TLS
# backend is mbedTLS-via-curl, not OpenSSL. SSH clone/fetch/push (Phase 86b) is
# served by the separate `ssh`/dropbear port via `GIT_SSH`; the SSH transport is
# orthogonal to git's curl linkage, so this same HTTPS-capable git binary serves
# both transports.
#
# git's build is plain-Makefile (not autotools `./configure`), so the cross is
# driven entirely by `CC=x86_64-linux-musl-gcc` — there is no `--host` flag to
# pass. Dependencies: zlib (object/pack compression) + curl (HTTPS transport,
# transitively pulling mbedtls + ca-certificates). The solver resolves the
# dependency-first order zlib -> mbedtls -> ca-certificates -> curl -> git
# (ca-certificates is curl's runtime trust store, so it precedes curl).
# zlib is consumed via git's `ZLIB_PATH`; curl via `CURL_CFLAGS`/`CURL_LDFLAGS`
# (the static libcurl+mbedtls+zlib link line). SHA-1/SHA-256 are git built-ins.
#
# Build knobs (see build_git in xtask/src/port_build.rs):
#   (NO_CURL removed)      — curl is LINKED for HTTPS smart-HTTP transport.
#   NO_OPENSSL=1           — TLS backend is mbedTLS-via-curl, not OpenSSL.
#   NO_GETTEXT=1           — no i18n message catalogs.
#   NO_TCLTK=1             — no gitk / git-gui.
#   NO_PERL=1 NO_PYTHON=1  — drop the scripted subcommands; the core C builtins
#                            (init/add/commit/log/diff/status/branch/merge/
#                            checkout) need neither.
#   NO_ICONV=1 NEEDS_LIBICONV= — no charset conversion (musl ships no libiconv).
#   NO_EXPAT=1             — drops the otherwise-pulled-in expat dependency
#                            (only used by the dumb-HTTP transport we don't build).
#   NO_REGEX=NeedsStartEnd — use git's bundled regex rather than musl's.
